{
  "dom_id": "step-607431",
  "name": "Quadrants in the Coordinate Plane",
  "problem": "The axes split the coordinate plane into four parts, called **quadrants**.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/938125e855fcb96f743c01f2a00d289ef13e0601772bab56cf0f255e9adf4dcd.png)\n\nGoing counter-clockwise, it's common to call\n\n- the top-right quadrant the first quadrant (I),\n\n- the top-left is the second quadrant (II),\n\n- the bottom-left is the third quadrant (III),\n\n- and and bottom-right is the fourth quadrant (IV).\n\nTo remember the order of the quadrants, it's helpful to think about writing the letter \"C\" in the graph:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/1ef91f2bc25ea8b887ec449d2dafe2eaf6a157733e7bc50e4480280df8190728.png)",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-607431\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"607431\" steptype=\"tutorial\" contentid=\"2097\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-607431\" class=\"stepAnchor\" name=\"step-13\">Quadrants in the Coordinate Plane</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"607431\">?</div>\n            </div> \n\n            <p>The axes split the coordinate plane into four parts, called <strong>quadrants</strong>.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-b548628fdc6184455a3aba4acbe1e957\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/b548628fdc6184455a3aba4acbe1e957\"></div>\n\n<p>Going counter-clockwise, it's common to call</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>the top-right quadrant the <span style=\"color:#2C72AE\">first quadrant</span> (I),</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>the top-left is the <span style=\"color:#E69F00\">second quadrant</span> (II),</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>the bottom-left is the <span style=\"color:#459B76\">third quadrant</span> (III),</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>and and bottom-right is the <span style=\"color:#C86426\">fourth quadrant</span> (IV).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>To remember the order of the quadrants, it's helpful to think about writing the letter \"C\" in the graph:</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-cc1f1203493d21743c7b80d5938157d1\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/cc1f1203493d21743c7b80d5938157d1\"></div>\n        </div>",
